==English==
{{wikipedia|Aldersgate#John Wesley|Aldersgate}}
===Etymology===
Short for {{w|Aldersgate Street}}, the site of a Moravian meeting at which {{w|John Wesley}} had a religious experience

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# A religious experience of {{w|John Wesley}}.
#* {{quote-journal| author={{w|John Wesley}} |journal=Journal| year=1738 | date=24 May 1738| passage=In the evening I went unwillingly to a society in '''Aldersgate''' Street, where one was reading Luther and preface to the Epistle to the Romans. About a quarter to nine, while he was describing the change which God works in the heart through faith in Christ, I felt my heart strangely warmed. I felt I did trust in Christ, Christ alone for salvation, and an assurance was given me that he had taken away my sins, even mine and saved me from the law of sin and death.}}